<?xml version="1.0"?>
<psalm
    errorLevel="5"
    resolveFromConfigFile="true"
    findUnusedBaselineEntry="true"
    findUnusedCode="false"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config"
    xsi:schemaLocation="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config vendor/vimeo/psalm/config.xsd"
>
    <!-- S444 — tests/ split out of psalm.xml into its own config so the
         production corpus could return to errorLevel 1 without unpinning the
         test tree. errorLevel is per-config in psalm 6.x (no per-directory
         override exists), so S306's single shared config meant ONE level for
         both corpora; the split keeps both promises at once:
         src + scripts @ 1 (psalm.xml), tests/ @ 5 (here).

         errorLevel="5" remains S306's deliberate, MEASURED choice, not a
         baseline — Psalm findings over tests/ (branch tree, analysis
         extensions loaded, the show-info=false flag, matching CI's command):

             level 1: 826   level 2: 623   level 3: 177   level 4: 155
             level 5:  30   level 6:  24   level 7:   7

         Levels 1-4 are dominated by findings that argue with TEST idiom rather
         than reporting defects: PropertyNotSetInConstructor x266 (PHPUnit
         initialises in setUp(), not __construct), InternalMethod x38
         (TestCase::addToAssertionCount is PHPUnit's public-but-@internal
         counting API), RedundantCast/RedundantCondition/TypeDoesNotContainType
         x~120 (deliberate runtime guards on decoded JSON and mixed socket
         payloads — the same defensive-code cliff that made phlix-server pin
         its Psalm level at 5), and Mixed* x~200 (json_decode trees asserted
         per-node via DecodedJsonAssertions). All 30 level-5 findings were
         FIXED honestly (undefined `use` variables, wrong interface docblock
         refinements, negative-offset reads, a Psalm-unparseable intersection
         return type, a property-reference capture, and one psalm-5.x
         array-shape inference quirk — a try/finally scope that also mutates
         captured-closure properties infers return-literal keys as OPTIONAL;
         fixed by assembling the shape in a clean typed helper, verified with
         a minimal repro). Raise the level if and when test doubles adopt
         typed row fixtures; do NOT add a psalm-baseline.xml or an
         <IssueHandler>, which would reproduce the "gate that proves nothing"
         defect S146 removed on phlix-server.

         Findings inside src/ and scripts/ files are NOT reported by this
         config even though psalm reads them for cross-boundary type
         inference: projectFiles is the report corpus, and production reports
         at the stricter level 1 in psalm.xml.

         Scope/level/commands are asserted by
         tests/Unit/Support/StaticAnalysisScopeTest.php. Venue PHP is 8.3.6
         (Psalm needs >= 8.3.16 to boot) — CI's "Psalm Static Analysis" check
         is authoritative; local reproduction ran in the s306-style docker
         mirror (php 8.3.33 + swoole 6.2.2 + pcntl/posix/pdo_mysql, no php-ast). -->
    <projectFiles>
        <directory name="tests"/>
        <ignoreFiles>
            <directory name="vendor"/>
            <!-- S306: the cross-repo route-manifest dumper boots sibling phlix-server
                 classes (Phlix\Server\*, Phlix\Common\Container\ContainerFactory) that do
                 not exist in this repo's autoloader — genuinely unanalysable here
                 (UndefinedClass/ForbiddenCode/shell-exec artifacts), the same written-why
                 exclusion PHPStan carries in phpstan.neon.dist excludePaths. -->
            <file name="tests/Unit/Http/Controllers/Fixtures/dump-phlix-server-route-manifest.php"/>
        </ignoreFiles>
    </projectFiles>
</psalm>
